{"packet_id":"D079-01","doc_id":"D079","jurisdiction":"San Francisco, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rent Ordinance just cause eviction requirement","requirement":"To evict a tenant from a unit covered by the Rent Ordinance, a landlord must have a just cause reason that is the dominant motive; expiration of the rental agreement or a change in ownership is not just cause.","key_value":"17 just cause reasons","coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the Rent Ordinance, including tenancies exempt from its rent increase limitations, such as units first certified for occupancy after June 13, 1979 and Costa-Hawkins-eligible tenancies.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the SF Rent Ordinance; covers some tenancies exempt from rent increase limits"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A landlord who evicts or tries to evict a tenant unlawfully may be subject to substantial civil and/or criminal liability.","effective_date":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code § 37.9","quoted_span":"In order to evict a tenant from a rental unit covered by the Rent Ordinance, a landlord must have a \"just cause\" reason that is the dominant motive for pursuing the eviction. Note that the mere expiration of a rental agreement or a change in ownership does not constitute \"just cause\" for eviction.","interaction":"Tenancies exempt from the Ordinance's rent increase limitations, including Costa-Hawkins-eligible tenancies, remain subject to its eviction provisions.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D079-01","doc_id":"D079","jurisdiction":"San Francisco, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Just cause required to remove housing services","requirement":"A landlord needs a just cause reason to take away or remove access to housing services such as garage, parking, driveway, storage and laundry facilities, though parking and storage may be temporarily removed for mandatory soft-story seismic retrofit work.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the Rent Ordinance and their housing services; temporary removal permitted where the landlord complies with Ordinance Section 37.2(r).","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Housing services attached to Rent Ordinance-covered units"},"exemptions":"Temporary removal of parking and storage spaces to perform mandatory soft-story seismic retrofit work required by the Building Code, if the landlord complies with Ordinance Section 37.2(r).","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code § 37.2","quoted_span":"The landlord also needs a \"just cause“ reason to take away or remove access to certain housing services, including but not limited to garage facilities, parking facilities, driveways, storage spaces, and laundry rooms.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
